[EXECUTING python]:
revenue_model = """================================================================================
                    REVENUE MODEL DESIGN: Invoice Follow-Up SaaS
                         (Solo Founder B2B Product)
================================================================================

1. BEST-FIT PRIMARY MODEL: TIERED SUBSCRIPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rationale: Matches the goal of predictable monthly revenue with minimal billing
complexity. Freelance accountants and tiny agencies expect SaaS pricing.

TIER STRUCTURE (Monthly Billing):
+-----------------+---------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| Tier            | Price   | Features                                            |
+-----------------+---------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| Starter         | $29/mo  | - Up to 50 invoices tracked                         |
|                 |         | - Email follow-ups (2 reminders)                    |
|                 |         | - Basic reporting                                   |
+-----------------+---------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| Pro (Recommended)| $79/mo | - Up to 250 invoices tracked                        |
|                 |         | - Email + SMS follow-ups (4 reminders)              |
|                 |         | - Custom branding                                   |
|                 |         | - CSV/Excel export                                  |
+-----------------+---------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| Agency          | $199/mo | - Up to 1000 invoices tracked                       |
|                 |         | - Unlimited follow-ups                              |
|                 |         | - Multi-user access (3 seats)                       |
|                 |         | - API access                                        |
|                 |         | - Priority support                                  |
+-----------------+---------+-----------------------------------------------------+

Why This Works:
- Clear value progression based on invoice volume (natural growth metric)
- $79/mo Pro tier targets the "sweet spot" for small agencies
- No complex usage metering; simple tier-based caps
- Annual discount option (2 months free) can be added later


2. SECONDARY REVENUE STREAMS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A) One-Time Template Pack: $49
   - Pre-built email/SMS templates for different scenarios
   - Industry-specific templates (construction, retail, professional services)
   - Evergreen add-on; zero ongoing support cost

B) Optional Onboarding Setup: $199 (one-time)
   - Import existing client data
   - Configure reminder schedules
   - 30-min kickoff call
   - Keep this optional; don't bundle into core pricing

C) White-Label Add-On: +$50/mo
   - Remove all product branding
   - Custom domain for client-facing emails
   - For agencies serving their own clients


3. PAYMENT FLOW (Solo-Founder Friendly Stack)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Recommended Stack: Stripe + Stripe Tax (or Paddle/LemonSqueezy for global)
Why: Both handle VAT, sales tax, and global payments automatically

Payment Flow:
1. User signs up -> free 14-day trial (no credit card required)
2. Trial ends -> redirect to Stripe Checkout (pre-built pricing page)
3. Payment succeeds -> webhook triggers account activation
4. Monthly charge -> automatic via Stripe subscription
5. Failed payment -> Stripe dunning (3 retry attempts over 8 days)
6. Churn -> downgrade to free tier or account pause

Solo-Founder Setup Checklist:
[] Create Stripe account (test mode first)
[] Configure webhook endpoints for subscription events
[] Set up Stripe Pricing Table component (no-code pricing page)
[] Enable automatic tax calculation (Stripe Tax)
[] Configure dunning management in Stripe Dashboard
[] Add revenue recognition tracking (simple spreadsheet at first)


4. 12-MONTH REVENUE PROJECTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Assumptions:
- Launch with 10 beta users (free during trial period)
- 3% monthly conversion from free trial to paid
- 5% monthly churn rate
- Average Revenue Per User (ARPU): $65 (weighted across tiers)
- Marketing: organic + content (no paid ads initially)

+--------+-------+---------+--------+--------+------------------+
| Month  | New   | Churned | Active | MRR    | Annualized (ARR) |
|        | Paid  |         | Subs   |        |                  |
+--------+-------+---------+--------+--------+------------------+
| 1      | 3     | 0       | 3      | $195   | $2,340           |
| 2      | 5     | 0       | 8      | $520   | $6,240           |
| 3      | 7     | 1       | 14     | $910   | $10,920          |
| 4      | 9     | 1       | 22     | $1,430 | $17,160          |
| 5      | 11    | 1       | 32     | $2,080 | $24,960          |
| 6      | 13    | 2       | 43     | $2,795 | $33,540          |
| 7      | 15    | 2       | 56     | $3,640 | $43,680          |
| 8      | 17    | 3       | 70     | $4,550 | $54,600          |
| 9      | 19    | 3       | 86     | $5,590 | $67,080          |
| 10     | 21    | 4       | 103    | $6,695 | $80,340          |
| 11     | 23    | 5       | 121    | $7,865 | $94,380          |
| 12     | 25    | 6       | 140    | $9,100 | $109,200         |
+--------+-------+---------+--------+--------+------------------+

Year 1 Totals:
- Total Revenue: ~$56,500 (cumulative MRR)
- Ending MRR: $9,100
- Ending ARR: $109,200
- Total Customers (active): 140

Secondary Stream Contribution (Estimate):
- Template Pack: 15% of new subs -> ~$3,500 Year 1
- Setup Services: 5% of new subs -> ~$2,000 Year 1
- Total Secondary: ~$5,500

GRAND TOTAL YEAR 1: ~$62,000


5. IMPLEMENTATION TIMELINE (Solo Founder)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Week 1: Set up Stripe, configure webhooks, create pricing page
Week 2: Build subscription management UI (upgrade/downgrade/cancel)
Week 3: Implement trial flow and dunning emails
Week 4: Soft launch to beta users, validate pricing
Month 2: Add template pack as digital download
Month 3: Introduce annual billing option (20% discount)
Month 6: Evaluate agency tier demand; consider white-label add-on


6. KEY METRICS TO TRACK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- MRR (Monthly Recurring Revenue)
- Churn Rate (target: <5% monthly)
- CAC (Customer Acquisition Cost)
- LTV (Lifetime Value; target: >$600 at 5% monthly churn)
- Trial-to-Paid Conversion (target: >3%)
- Expansion Revenue (upsells from Starter -> Pro -> Agency)


7. RISK MITIGATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Pricing Risk: Start with lower prices; test elasticity in Month 3
- Churn Risk: Add win-back emails and pause (vs. cancel) option
- Billing Risk: Use Stripe/Paddle to handle compliance; no DIY invoicing
- Cash Flow Risk: Keep fixed costs low; reinvest first $20K ARR


================================================================================
                              SUMMARY
================================================================================
PRIMARY MODEL:  3-tier monthly subscription ($29/$79/$199)
SECONDARY:      Template pack ($49), onboarding ($199), white-label (+$50/mo)
PAYMENT STACK:  Stripe + Stripe Tax (or Paddle/LemonSqueezy for global)
YEAR 1 GOAL:    $62,000 revenue ($9,100 MRR by Month 12)
COMPLEXITY:     Low - automated billing, no usage metering, no marketplace
================================================================================
"""

with open('/workspace/revenue_model.md', 'w') as f:
    f.write(revenue_model)

print("Revenue model written to /workspace/revenue_model.md")

